From 29afd93d02e5303c923d0bfc52bd2cb4275f9300 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:50:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] net: hix5hd2: keep a fixed link off the MDIO child scan

A node that declares a fixed link has no PHY address, yet
of_mdiobus_register() treated every child without a reg property as a
PHY candidate: it warns about the missing address, then walks all 32
addresses printing a line each.

Register the bus with the scan masked out when the node declares a fixed
link, the same mask of_mdiobus_register() applies before it parses its
children, so the lifecycle of the bus pointer stays as it is. With the
mask applied the 33 lines are not printed and eth0 still registers with
the address from the device tree.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
@@ -1189,7 +1189,18 @@ static int hix5hd2_dev_probe(struct plat
 	snprintf(bus->id, MII_BUS_ID_SIZE, "%s-mii", dev_name(&pdev->dev));
 	priv->bus = bus;
 
-	ret = of_mdiobus_register(bus, node);
+	/*
+	 * A fixed link names no PHY on this bus, and of_mdiobus_register() would
+	 * treat the fixed-link child as a PHY candidate with no reg property and
+	 * walk all 32 addresses printing a line per address, so register the bus
+	 * with the scan masked out instead.
+	 */
+	if (of_phy_is_fixed_link(node)) {
+		bus->phy_mask = ~0;
+		ret = mdiobus_register(bus);
+	} else {
+		ret = of_mdiobus_register(bus, node);
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_free_mdio;
 
